{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>You shall not boil a kid in its mother's milk.</b> I have already explained this verse at the end of the section Ki Tissa, and I need not repeat it here. And it is stated in the Torah three times: one for the prohibition of eating, one for the prohibition of deriving benefit, and one for the prohibition of cooking. And in tractate Ḥullin: 'a kid' and not a wild animal; 'a kid' and not a fowl; 'a kid' and not an unclean beast — it comes to teach us that there is in them no prohibition of meat in milk by Torah law."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:48:16.317274510Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}